# Applies to every service in docker-compose.yml -- all four builds use this
# directory (community/) as their build context, with `dockerfile:
# apps/<app>/Dockerfile`, precisely so this one file covers all of them.
#
# Without this, `COPY apps/<app>/. .` in each Dockerfile would ship whatever
# node_modules/.next/out/dist already exist on the host checkout (macOS
# binaries, stale builds) into the Linux build stage, silently shadowing the
# COPY --from=deps node_modules layer that npm ci just produced correctly.

**/node_modules
**/.next
**/out
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/coverage

**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
!**/.env.example

**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/*.log
npm-debug.log*

**/.DS_Store
**/*.tsbuildinfo

**/.vscode
**/.idea

# Local artifact storage written by the API's default STORAGE_DRIVER=local
# driver (config.ts -> storage.localDir "./data/artifacts"). It is gitignored
# host-only state (see .gitignore "Runtime artifacts and local data"), and
# `COPY apps/api/. .` in the api build stage would otherwise bake whatever a
# developer has uploaded locally into the image and invalidate the build cache
# on every upload. The runner stage creates an empty, correctly-owned
# data/artifacts itself.
apps/api/data/
